phy: qcom: qmp-combo: keep usb_init_count across the DP-only mux switch

The Type-C mux transition path decrements qmp->usb_init_count whenever it
switches the combo PHY to QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY:

	if (new_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY) {
		if (qmp->usb_init_count)
			qmp->usb_init_count--;
	}

but no USB PHY consumer has called .exit() here. The mux going DP-only is
not the same event as dwc3 releasing the USB PHY. usb_init_count is owned
by qmp_combo_usb_init() / qmp_combo_usb_exit(); adjusting it from the mux
path desyncs the software refcount from actual consumer ownership, so a
later mode transition or a suspend/resume cycle powers the USB PHY on or
off out of step (or skips it via the `if (!qmp->usb_init_count)` guard a
few lines further down this same function).

Drop the DP-only decrement. Requested PHY mode is independent of consumer
reference ownership.

--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4512,11 +4512,6 @@
 		/* Now everything's powered down, power up the right PHYs */
 		qmp_combo_com_init(qmp, true);
 
-		if (new_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY) {
-			if (qmp->usb_init_count)
-				qmp->usb_init_count--;
-		}
-
 		if (new_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_USB3DP || new_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_USB3_ONLY) {
 			qmp_combo_usb_power_on(qmp->usb_phy);
 			if (!qmp->usb_init_count)
